  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 21-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 stack on fused silica substrate under normal incidence. Initialize all layer thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness for 267.5 nm center wavelength (HfO2: n≈2.05 at 267.5 nm gives ~32.7 nm physical thickness; SiO2: n≈1.48 at 267.5 nm gives ~45.2 nm physical thickness). Apply optimization bounds of ±8% around these quarter-wave targets for each layer. Stack sequence: Air | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | Fused silica. Optimize layer thicknesses to maximize mean transmittance in 255-280 nm band while minimizing mean transmittance in 300-700 nm and 700-1100 nm bands. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 255–280 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Transmittance in 300–700 nm; Transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: Maximum 30 layers; No metal layers; Only conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize 20 alternating HfO2/SiO2 layers on fused silica under normal incidence to maximize mean transmittance in 255–280 nm while minimizing mean transmittance in 300–700 nm and 700–1100 nm, with ±8% thickness bounds around quarter-wave thicknesses at 267.5 nm.",
